-- title:
--   Pinned endomorphism acts by substitution of the series S
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $A$ a scheme and $f\colon A\to\operatorname{Spec}K$, and let $L$ be a relative group law on $f$, i.e. a functorially compatible group structure on the sets $\{\varphi\colon T\to A \mid \varphi\circ f=t\}$ of $A$-points over bases $t\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}K$. Fix $n\in\mathbb N$, a two-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $K$, and a system of formal coordinates $\theta$ of rank $2$ for $f$ (for each $K$-algebra $B'$ a map from pairs in $B'$ to points of $A$ over $\operatorname{Spec}B'$) which satisfies `L.IsFormalCoordinates F θ`: $\theta$ is natural in $K$-algebra maps on nilpotent tuples, and for each ideal $J$ with $J^{n+1}=0$ it carries tuples in $J$ bijectively onto the points infinitesimally close to the identity and transports the truncated law $F.\mathrm{nilMul}$ to $L.\mathrm{mul}$. Let $\varphi\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,2\to K[[X_1,X_2]]$, let $H$ be a commutative $K$-Hopf algebra together with bijections $e_T$, natural-free, from the type synonym `WithConv` of $K$-algebra maps $H\to T$ onto the set of $n$-torsion points of $L$ over $\operatorname{Spec}T$, let $\nu\in\mathbb N$ and let $\Phi\colon K[[X_1,X_2]]/(\varphi_0,\varphi_1)\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }H$ be a $K$-algebra isomorphism pinned by the hypothesis that for every $K$-algebra $T$ and every $\chi\colon H\to T$, writing $c_\chi(i)=\chi(\Phi(\overline{X_i}))$: some ideal $J\subseteq T$ with $J^{\nu+1}=0$ contains all $c_\chi(i)$; $\chi(\Phi(\overline G))=\mathrm{nilEval}_\nu(G)(c_\chi)$ for all $G$, where $\mathrm{nilEval}_\nu$ evaluates the truncation of $G$ in all degrees $\le\nu$; and $e_T(\chi)=\theta_T(c_\chi)$ as points over $\operatorname{Spec}T$. Let $\mathrm{act}\colon A\to A$ be a morphism and $S\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,2\to K[[X_1,X_2]]$ a pair of series with zero constant terms such that for every $K$-algebra $T$, every ideal $J$ with $J^{m+1}=0$ and every tuple $s$ in $J$ the underlying morphism of $\theta_T(\mathrm{nilEval}_m(S_i)(s))_i$ equals that of $\theta_T(s)$ followed by $\mathrm{act}$. Let $\varphi^\sharp\colon H\to H$ be a $K$-algebra endomorphism such that for all $T$ and all $\chi$ the underlying morphism of $e_T(\chi\circ\varphi^\sharp)$ equals that of $e_T(\chi)$ followed by $\mathrm{act}$. Then for every $G\in K[[X_1,X_2]]$ one has $\varphi^\sharp(\Phi(\overline G))=\Phi(\overline{G(S_0,S_1)})$, the bar denoting the class modulo the ideal generated by the $\varphi_i$ and $G(S_0,S_1)$ being `MvPowerSeries.subst S G`.
--
--   This is the transport step identifying, under a pinned coordinate presentation $H\cong K[[X_1,X_2]]/(\varphi)$ of the Hopf algebra of $n$-torsion points of a relative group law, an endomorphism of $H$ matched with a scheme endomorphism $\mathrm{act}$ of $A$ with substitution of the tuple of series $S$ expressing $\mathrm{act}$ in the formal coordinates $\theta$. It is used in the construction of the special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module attached to a fake elliptic curve in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting.
